{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes","id":1099881,"title":"The Origins of the Fifteen Tribes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-03T12:15:05-07:00","id":1099881,"title":"The Origins of the Fifteen Tribes","content":"Garou are hybrids of humans and gray wolves, which histrionically existed throughout all of Europe and the majority of Asia and North America, so it would make sense for the Garou to have existed anywhere there were wild gray wolf population. Among the Garou, one tribe was unambiguously Asia (Stargazer), one tribe was unambiguously Australian origin (Bunyip), one tribe was unambiguously North Africa (Silent Striders), three tribes were unambiguously European origin (Fianna, Get of Fenris, and White Howlers), and three tribes were unambiguously North American (Croatan, Uktenu, and Wendigo). Of the remaining seven Tribes, however, they seem to actually have an Asian origin, which I will explain.<br /> <br /> Black Furies are Amazons, which were historically associated with Scythian tribes of Central Asia, and probably migrated from Central Asia into Europe during prehistory. Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers seem to have originated in West Asia, with the rise of the city-states of the Middle East, and migrated into East Asia and South Asia after the establishment of the Silk Road and into Europe during the rise of the Roman Empire. The Silver Fangs and the Shadow Lords both seem to have originated in North Asia (the existence of the Siberakh offers evidence of the North Asian origin of the Silver Fangs while the existence of the Hakken offers evidence of the North Asian origin of the Shadow Lords) and migrated into Central Asia (and through Central Asia into Europe) and East Asia and South Asia during prehistory. The Children of Gaia are probably the original South Asian Tribe of Garou, though I am not sure. as their origins seem to be much more fuzzy. The Red Talons would have also likely been Asian in origin, there was four times as much wolf habitat in Asia than in Europe, though they would have likely spread into Europe during prehistory.<br /> <br /> The Garou Nation would just be the result of the European Garou conquering the North American Garou. The Garou outside of Europe and North America would either belong to the Beast Courts (if in East Asia) or local tribal organizations. I am curious if anyone sees anything wrong with my analysis or if you would like to present an alternative analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T12:27:36-07:00","id":1099883,"title":"","content":"Have you had a chance to read Shattered Dreams yet? it actually has a section on the migration of the Garou out of Africa into Asia. It also talks about the prehistoric tribes that later became the modern day tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T12:53:21-07:00","id":1099892,"title":"","content":"I never liked Shattered Dreams because it is supposed to be non-canon, which means that it might as well not even exist. Anyway, the Garou could not have originated in Africa because gray wolves never existed in Africa. Come to think of it, Silent Striders would have had to evolved outside of Africa because of that and migrated into North Africa during prehistory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:19:26-07:00","id":1099913,"title":"","content":"I prefer a creationist origin for Garou, especially when it comes to the Three Brothers.<br /> To protect and watch over the Pure Lands, Gaia created Eldest Brother from Water and Wisdom so that he would be clever and flexible enough to contend with the schemes of the Defiler Wyrm, Middle Brother out of Earth and Honor so that he would be stoic and virtuous enough to resist the temptations of the Eater of Souls, and Youngest Brother out of Wind and Glory so that he would be ferocious and fast enough to battle the Beast of War. And to assist them she created the Three Sisters out of Fire, Stone and Water to compliment the Three Brothers. (And, obviously, the North American Bastet say this is wrong; Gaia created the Three Brothers to assist them, not the other way around.) Because the idea that The People came over some land bridge instead of up out from the Third World is clearly some sort of European silliness based on lies told them by Old Man Coyote. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:44:05-07:00","id":1099922,"title":"","content":"I go with the idea that Garou history is as full of BS and lies and some small truths as any other creation mythology. They don't KNOW their history and that kind of troubles them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:44:18-07:00","id":1099923,"title":"","content":"Which is just as valid as any other Creation myth, though it does ignore the Corax, Mokole, Nuwisha, etc. On another note, people have argued that the Nuwisha should be considered to be Garou, since coyotes produce fertile offspring with wolves, just that they would have been a Tribe who gave up Rage (and the weakness to silver) to gain a greater connection to the Umbra during prehistory (before the War of Rage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T15:41:21-07:00","id":1099936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099922#post1099922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I go with the idea that Garou history is as full of BS and lies and some small truths as any other creation mythology. They don't KNOW their history and that kind of troubles them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you've said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T16:01:04-07:00","id":1099940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099936#post1099936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So you've said.</div> </div> </div> </div>You realize that's kind of canon, right? You keep trying to say the Garou know everything and the problem is all the tribebooks say different stories so it's flat out impossible for all of them to be right.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T18:55:27-07:00","id":1099975,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between folk tales and objective truths. The Garou can always learn objective truths by talking to the correct spirits, but they prefer their folk tales because they want comforting lies instead of hard truths. It is a bit like the people who deny science by rejecting global climate change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T19:17:15-07:00","id":1099984,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099923#post1099923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is just as valid as any other Creation myth, though it does ignore the Corax, Mokole, Nuwisha, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Brother Raven, Grandfather Alligator, Brother Coyote, Mother Bear, Grandmother Spider, Brother Bat, Grandfather Rattlesnake, Those Annoying Rat People ....<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T19:56:55-07:00","id":1099992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099923#post1099923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is just as valid as any other Creation myth, though it does ignore the Corax, Mokole, Nuwisha, etc. On another note, people have argued that the Nuwisha should be considered to be Garou, since coyotes produce fertile offspring with wolves, just that they would have been a Tribe who gave up Rage (and the weakness to silver) to gain a greater connection to the Umbra during prehistory (before the War of Rage).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Nuwisha are Garou in the same way the Bunyip were and that new tribe is. The Garou are just being racist again.<br /> <br /> As for the spirits, I pointed out they're greatly shaped by their natures, the oddity of the Umbra's relationship to time, metaphor, and the prejudices of the viewer/spirit. Many spirits appear differently to different Garou and speak in metaphor when they're not outright lying. It doesn't help the Garou's patron spirit, Luna, is a figure of constant change as well as lunacy.<br /> <br /> So, no, I don't think it's a matter of simply going up to Griffon and asking, &quot;So what's the real story?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-03-2017, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T22:16:27-07:00","id":1100010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099975#post1099975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between folk tales and objective truths. The Garou can always learn objective truths by talking to the correct spirits, but they prefer their folk tales because they want comforting lies instead of hard truths. It is a bit like the people who deny science by rejecting global climate change.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) People who reject climate change aren't clining to a comforting lie. They're clinging to what they perceive as the &quot;real threat&quot; - government control. They're absolutely full of shit, but it's because they're paranoid about the wrong threat, not because the lie makes them feel safer.<br /> <br /> 2) Werewolves who seek it out get conflicting stories from spirits who often perceive events in alien metaphoric ways through the lens of their own specific natures. The game does not so disrespect the tradition of oral history as to portray it as a &quot;comforting lie&quot; in conflict with accessible truth - it's the strongest tether to the past the Garou have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-04-2017, 02:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T04:42:36-07:00","id":1100071,"title":"","content":"A minor question related tangentially to the thread, but just how candid <i>are </i>spirits over here anyway? Especially when it comes to things that aren't their immediate concerns, like shapeshifter history. I come from ChroD, where spirits are only <i>sometimes </i>sacred guardians of nature, and most of them just don't give a damn about anything else that doesn't concern their purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T06:44:51-07:00","id":1100100,"title":"","content":"It depends on the spirit. Most Incarna probably know the truth, but they will probably not share it without good reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T09:26:41-07:00","id":1100160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100071#post1100071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A minor question related tangentially to the thread, but just how candid <i>are </i>spirits over here anyway? Especially when it comes to things that aren't their immediate concerns, like shapeshifter history. I come from ChroD, where spirits are only <i>sometimes </i>sacred guardians of nature, and most of them just don't give a damn about anything else that doesn't concern their purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>I view spirits as heavily biased by their nature and those that are above it, inclined to embellish the truth. I also think spirits may well not REMEMBER it perfectly as well since nothing says Jupiter is inclined to think of the past in an objective manner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T10:40:09-07:00","id":1100174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100010#post1100010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) People who reject climate change aren't clining to a comforting lie. They're clinging to what they perceive as the &quot;real threat&quot; - government control. They're absolutely full of shit, but it's because they're paranoid about the wrong threat, not because the lie makes them feel safer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the last time the progressive technocratic elites of academia and government were this religiously enamored with a &quot;settled&quot; scientific theory, it was eugenics, and absolutely nothing bad came from that, did it.<br /> <br /> (And most climate change &quot;deniers&quot; - and isn't that a nice phrase of religious orthodoxy - are perfectly accepting of the idea that climate changes - the Medieval Warm Period and the following Little Ice Age are pretty well documented - but question how much impact human activity has on it, or if the effects of any theoretical change would be more or less harmful that the poverty and misery resulting from the sort of command and control economies insisted on as possible solutions.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T11:07:41-07:00","id":1100179,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100174#post1100174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Because the last time the progressive technocratic elites of academia and government were this religiously enamored with a &quot;settled&quot; scientific theory, it was eugenics, and absolutely nothing bad came from that, did it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, that was also a very different group of people operating under a very different body of knowledge. To wit, they were trying to steer human evolution without actually knowing about how a lot of mechanisms actually worked. In contrast, modern people know quite a great deal more about how climate works, and you can get the amount of hydrocarbon fuels burned straight from the industry's mouth to calculate how much shit you're in with some simple math problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And most climate change &quot;deniers&quot; - and isn't that a nice phrase of religious orthodoxy </div> </div> </div>No. They're denying numbers in front of them. That's not an orthodoxy, it's a series of math problems. Denying math problems is not a righteous struggle for freedom.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> are perfectly accepting of the idea that climate changes - the Medieval Warm Period and the following Little Ice Age are pretty well documented - but question how much impact human activity has on it, or if the effects of any theoretical change would be more or less harmful that the poverty and misery resulting from the sort of command and control economies insisted on as possible solutions.) </div> </div> </div>Well, the actual effects are that the amount of money that we're spending to keep New Orleans from flooding now is good metric for how much money we'll end up spending to make all the other coastal cities in the US not go underwater as quickly as other below-sea level places will. Meanwhile, lots of other people living on islands and in coastal areas without access to amazing amounts of wealth aren't going to have that luxury; they will drown outright in the imminent onlap sequence, or end up living in squalid misery further and further inland.<br /> <br /> And as for questioning human impact, that'd fly if humans weren't everywhere and in huge numbers on every continent but Antarctica. Much like how seemingly inconsequential and invisible microbes altered the atmosphere with the oxygen revolution. Besides, you can't liberate all the carbon stored up during the Permian and not expect it to have a rather profound effect on the world around you.<br /> <br /> If you want to know where the terrible conspiracy shit is, it's with the people insisting that we still use pent up Permian carbon. They're amazingly wealthy from an entire industry built on it, and they want to keep every last scrap of wealth. Decades ago, they were so hesitant to install catalytic converters that regulatory boards had to drag them kicking and screaming into it. Then the industry acted like it saved the world on its own. Want to keep bloated plutocratic industries/conspiracies from perpetuating their dominance when solar gets set up? Push to not monetize energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T11:12:12-07:00","id":1100180,"title":"","content":"It was the conservative and totalitarian elements of society that pushed for eugenics because they wanted a nice perfect white world. When it comes to science, scientists tend to be pretty attached to theories like gravity, plate tectonics, evolution, oxygen respiration, the heliocentric model, and sexual reproduction. Anthropogenic climate change is occurring and there is nothing that the climate change deniers can say that makes their position any more scientific that the people who deny the Moon Landing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T11:21:39-07:00","id":1100181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100180#post1100180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was the conservative and totalitarian elements of society that pushed for eugenics because they wanted a nice perfect white world. When it comes to science, scientists tend to be pretty attached to theories like gravity, plate tectonics, evolution, oxygen respiration, the heliocentric model, and sexual reproduction. Anthropogenic climate change is occurring and there is nothing that the climate change deniers can say that makes their position any more scientific that the people who deny the Moon Landing.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was white progressives of the era. The SOCIALISTS were largely against it, as they saw social ills as being caused by external oppression rather than genetic failings (a cornerstone of hardline eugenics) or overpopulation (moderate eugenics). But white progressives ala Teddy Roosevelt and Henry Ford and Nikolai Tesla were leaders of the movement.<br /> <br /> But it is indeed a false conflation between modern racially diverse progressives and the white movement of that era.<br /> <br /> Anyway what's notable here is that &quot;No One of Consequence&quot; didn't provide any peer reviewed scientific evidence to contradict man-made climate change, because none exists.<br /> <br /> The Koch brothers funding research by an outspoken climate skeptic still confirmed all the consensus conclusions! The deniers of man-made climate change have all the funding they could ever want from the fossil fuel industry if they could produce contrary research that stands up to scrutiny, but they can't. They've got nothing so they have to fall back on conspiracy theories and innuendo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 06-04-2017, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T14:50:02-07:00","id":1100223,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I see nothing unlikely about a Galliard being told by Jacob Morningkill to write an epic ballad about how the War of Rage was started by evil Fera who kidnapped baby werewolf cubs to drink their blood in rituals to the service of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> I think it's canon the Wendigo believe the whole &quot;Pure Lands&quot; business and pretend Native tribes weren't up to all manner of violence and strife like the rest of the world. You know, despite archaeological evidence proving otherwise. Also, the Uktena claiming otherwise.<br /> <br /> Garou are a oral tradition warrior society and history has shown they were no more stranger to propaganda than modern humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 06-04-2017, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:27:04-07:00","id":1100470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100223#post1100223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's canon the Wendigo believe the whole &quot;Pure Lands&quot; business and pretend Native tribes weren't up to all manner of violence and strife like the rest of the world. You know, despite archaeological evidence proving otherwise. Also, the Uktena claiming otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is quite cannon that the Uktena and Wendigo claim they did not participate in the Impergium *at all*, yet somehow neither of them are the Tribe with the reduced Delirium Flaw...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T10:17:05-07:00","id":1100488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1099975#post1099975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is a difference between folk tales and objective truths. The Garou can always learn objective truths by talking to the correct spirits,</div> </div> </div> </div>Because spirits are well known for their objectivity and embrace of scientific consensus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:43:17-07:00","id":1100672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100470#post1100470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is quite cannon that the Uktena and Wendigo claim they did not participate in the Impergium *at all*, yet somehow neither of them are the Tribe with the reduced Delirium Flaw...</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the rules also say that a number of people around the world, such as First Nations peoples, don't suffer from the Delirium. It's probably structured that way because, though they didn't participate in it, the Uktena and Wendigo still look like the werewolves who did, so the other populations that were subjected to it still react to them as if they had.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T07:07:16-07:00","id":1100815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b