 to the effective Willpower of a witness, but the concept remains the same. Also, &quot;looks like&quot; in the context of Crinos means &quot;is a towering wolf-headed death machine on two legs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Coggies don't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T11:50:48-07:00","id":1100901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100842#post1100842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 page 263, and W:tA Revised page 192. Technically, it says a bonus to the effective Willpower of a witness, but the concept remains the same. Also, &quot;looks like&quot; in the context of Crinos means &quot;is a towering wolf-headed death machine on two legs&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> w20 says they didn't suffer &quot;to a great degree&quot; and only get a slight bonus much less than the COG 5 wp bonus across the board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 06-06-2017, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T15:47:19-07:00","id":1100991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1099881-the-origins-of-the-fifteen-tribes?p=1100901#post1100901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> w20 says they didn't suffer &quot;to a great degree&quot; and only get a slight bonus much less than the COG 5 wp bonus across the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20, the same book that doesn't include tribal weaknesses? That W20?<br /> <br /> We can't actually say that CoG have a &quot;pierced veil&quot;. Because the mechanic that it was tied to was basically a forced symmetry between Werewolf tribes and Vampire clans that never made sense. Hell, for half the year, the Wendigo &quot;weakness&quot; is a benefit! That's why they got dropped. I can even remember the blog post where the decision to drop them got made, way back in 2012. There weren't many willing to speak up on behalf of tribal weaknesses, in the end, and so we need not use them, ever.<br /> <br /> Besides, even the Fera who didn't participate in the Impergium still scare the shit out of people with a meager 2 point boost; this category includes Corax. It makes no sense for Children of Gaia not to inflict full Delirium, no matter how much they've tried to reconcile or how. They're Garou, and they still carry that weight.","signature":"","edited"